cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Daniel Longitudinal Study"
message: >
  If you use or reference this repository, please cite it using the
  metadata below. This archive documents a continuous single-subject
  longitudinal observation of training adaptation, recovery signals,
  and behavioral execution patterns.

type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: Hughett
    given-names: Christopher Daniel
    alias: CDHughett

repository-code: https://github.com/CDHughett/daniel-longitudinal-public

abstract: >
  The Daniel Longitudinal Study is a governed public archive documenting
  a continuous single-subject observation of training exposure, recovery
  dynamics, and system-level physiological adaptation over time.

keywords:
  - longitudinal observation
  - self quantification
  - training adaptation
  - recovery monitoring
  - human performance

